exed by Fin(l+1); conversely H006 supplies such a basis. Stability under all divided powers is equivalent to stability under the Z-algebra they generate, by closure under sums and compositions. With 0≤lam, l=lam.toNat equals lam. The canonical tensor flip identifies K tensor_Z M with M tensor_Z K in both directions and intertwines the tensor-induced operators; VK uses only the scalar-first representation. IntegralOps records restrictions agreeing on every lattice element and inherited brackets: they are unique by injectivity of M into V, and T007 constructs them from H004/H006, so its existential witness adds no premise and denotes the actual induced action. Nontrivial means nonzero, and bottom/top mean zero/the whole space. Invariance under the three generators is equivalent to invariance under the image of L(K), since they span it and W is K-linear; this needs no faithful action and remains valid for p=2 and lam=0. No algebraic closure hypothesis is imposed.\"}}},\"library_terms\":{}}}","status":"completed"}}

