≤ lam ∧ lam < (p : ℤ)) (h_H004 : Module.Finite ℂ V ∧ Module.finrank ℂ V = lam.toNat+1 ∧ LR.Brackets x y h ∧ Nontrivial V ∧ ∀ W : Submodule ℂ V, LR.Inv W x → LR.Inv W y → LR.Inv W h → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤) (h_H005 : v ≠ 0 ∧ x v = 0 ∧ h v = (lam : ℂ) • v) (h_H006 : (∃ f : Module.Basis (LR.Idx lam.toNat) ℤ M, ∃ c : Module.Basis (LR.Idx lam.toNat) ℂ V, ∀ i, (f i : V) = c i) ∧ (∀ r m, m ∈ M → LR.DP x r m ∈ M) ∧ (∀ r m, m ∈ M → LR.DP y r m ∈ M)), Nontrivial (LR.VK K M) ∧ ∃ o : LR.IntegralOps M x y h, ∀ W : Submodule K (LR.VK K M), LR.Inv W (o.xz.baseChange K) → LR.Inv W (o.yz.baseChange K) → LR.Inv W (o.hz.baseChange K) → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤\",\"correspondence\":{\"mode\":\"equivalent\",\"explanation\":\"The parameters retain every prime p, arbitrary field K of characteristic p, integer lam in [0,p), complex module, highest-weight vector and arbitrary admissible lattice. The Chevalley brackets present sl2(C): a triple of endomorphisms satisfying them defines its action, and every original action gives such a triple. Common invariant subspaces express irreducibility; H004 retains dimension and H005 supplies the highest-weight vector. A Z-submodule of V is equivalently an additive subgroup. By H004 its simultaneous integer/complex basis can be reindexed by Fin(l+1); conversely H006 supplies such a basis. Stability under all divided powers is equivalent to stability under the Z-algebra they generate, by closure under sums and compositions. With 0≤lam, l=lam.toNat equals lam. The canonical tensor flip identifies K tensor_Z M with M tensor_Z K in both directions and intertwines the tensor-induced operators; VK uses only the scalar-first representation. IntegralOps records restrictions agreeing on every lattice element and inherited brackets: they are unique by injectivity of M into V, and T007 constructs them from H004/H006, so its existential witness adds no premise and denotes the actual induced action. Nontrivial means nonzero, and bottom/top mean zero/the whole space. Invariance under the three generators is equivalent to invariance under the image of L(K), since they span it and W is K-linear; this needs no faithful action and remains valid for p=2 and lam=0. No algebraic closure hypothesis is imposed.\"}}},\"library_terms\":{}}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report an actual obstacle using these five direct fields. Countercheck the alleged implication against the complete definitions, quantifiers and inequality directions; a feasible example alone does not determine an extremum. A fact not yet proved or registered in the current draft is an obligation to complete, not by itself a gap. For a mathematical stop, identify the concrete implication and actual mathematical difficulty encountered during normal checking/completion, not merely unfilled inventory or exposition. No fixed time/attempt count or counterexample is required. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP/SUSPECTED_GAP stop for an actual supported mathematical obstruction; SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE/INPUT_CONFLICT stop for an actual access/input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished work is not an obstacle report. No mathematical acceptance is generated.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"